Subject: [PATCH v3 3/3] claude/skills/freebsd-port: Thread each revision under
 its first version
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: rkrlzwxwostolzxrwwzpsqlpnklxmsns
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:28:50 +0000

freebsd-port formats with plain git format-patch in a ports tree, so
format-patch.sh never picks the reply target there. It now says to
pass --in-reply-to with v1, so ports revisions thread like the rest
of the list.
---
change-id: rkrlzwxwostolzxrwwzpsqlpnklxmsns

 .claude/skills/freebsd-port/SKILL.md | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.claude/skills/freebsd-port/SKILL.md b/.claude/skills/freebsd-port/SKILL.md
index 7f7f8310..505741d1 100644
--- a/.claude/skills/freebsd-port/SKILL.md
+++ b/.claude/skills/freebsd-port/SKILL.md
@@ -215,6 +215,9 @@ If v(N-1) does not apply onto the new base, run series-rebuild.sh
 without `-o` and pass `--range-diff="${prev}"` instead; an interdiff
 across two bases would show every commit that landed between them.
 End the notes with what changed and a `Link to v(N-1):` line.
+Thread the revision under v1, as git.git has recommended since June
+2026, by adding `--in-reply-to=<message-id of v1>`, so every version
+of the port and its review stay in one thread.
 
 Deliver the series into the mail workspace and push it, as
 zib/patch-review-workflow.org describes:
